{"base_rate":0.09354413702239789,"brier":0.058189064558629766,"bss":0.31375666352767784,"bss_hi":0.4609626436518047,"bss_lo":0.13028696206237206,"chart":{"base":[183.3,148.4],"fp":[211.7,273.0],"lead":"62,256.9 272,231.9 482,199.5 692,162.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.31 — higher than 53% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +14pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 66% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 29% → rained 44%"},"rel":"64.3,463.1 245.8,278.1"},"country":"MX","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.031475625823451904,"ess":339.1882759073273,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tijuana</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tijuana rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (48%), believe about\n<b>62%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 759 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSAN DIEGO BROWN FLD, 8.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.31, ranked 63 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;117) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>474</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>131</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tijuana</b> <span class=\"muted\">MX</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.31</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;117\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>759 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tijuana &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tijuana\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 63.918015267175576,365.32824427480915 90.14320000000001,323.76 228.7713924050633,170.0506329113924 228.7713924050633,239.16455696202533 90.14320000000001,372.29333333333335 63.918015267175576,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"347.9499341238472\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"347.9499341238472\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,381.2320675105485 63.918015267175576,373.6641221374046 90.14320000000001,294.64 228.7713924050633,156.22784810126583\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 474 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"381.2320675105485\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 2%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 131 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"63.918015267175576\" cy=\"373.6641221374046\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"90.14320000000001\" cy=\"294.64\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"228.7713924050633\" cy=\"156.22784810126583\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(9%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tijuana the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.56) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.87).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>-1.866</td><td class='num'>5.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.326</td><td class='num'>8.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'>0.495</td><td class='num'>3.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.560</td><td class='num'>5.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":32.5027,"lon":-117.00371,"n":759,"n_cities":134,"name":"Tijuana","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":474,"obs":0.002109704641350211,"sig":true},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.0167175572519084,"n":131,"obs":0.022900763358778626,"sig":false},{"hi":0.17,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.0908,"n":75,"obs":0.24,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.17,"mean":0.48240506329113925,"n":79,"obs":0.620253164556962,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.1,"provisional":false,"rank":63,"rank_hi":117.02499999999998,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.004186866830530598,"resolution":0.037077184887244485,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"tijuana","station":"SAN DIEGO BROWN FLD","timezone":"America/Tijuana"}